**Definition 2.3 (actual raw decoder and finite patch table).** Form the
following finite enumeration, with no dependence on future capacities.
Enumerate absent/0/1 patterns of the fixed slot catalog, active version,
PC/mode/cursor, token/latch patterns, and all raw bit contents of each
fixed finite native version store. During a bootstrap the active rows
are its fixed NEXT/INPUT/WRITE/ADVANCE/DONE rows. A wrong supplied bit
changes its actual raw store, not that active bootstrap. After DONE use
ARC Definition 6.2's actual decoded row: no unique in-range well-typed
row means no enabled main row. A unique row uses its actual seven native
fields and ordered finite local effects, not the canonical $G$ row.

The row/effect interpreter is ARC Definition 6.2's finite grammar. In
particular a finite effect may preserve, assign a named finite bit from
a literal/designated latch, change a seal/mark at a named port's current
or immediately preceding existing marker, select a named stage/version,
advance its fixed finite cursor, halt, or select an F receipt. Its
arguments cannot be runtime words, addresses, lists or capacities.
Out-of-range ports, latches, symbols, Boolean tables, stages or slot
indices fail the same decoder/guard. An absent required location is not
read as 0. Native token/boundary/writability and cursor conditions are
tested as in the actual primitive domain. No new enabling permission
is supplied by the fact that a rule is in this enumeration.

For each decoded possibility, list its actual bounded cell roles and
walks in effect order, including every named CTL marker role, every moved-to
neighbor and the meter append cell. Enumerate their eight-track bytes,
endpoint aliases and the two raw IN values. The immediately preceding
marker uses the existing predecessor walk, subject to the same existence
guard; a control effect does not hide a seek to an encoded numeral.
Where an effect reads a value already changed by an earlier effect, use
that intermediate finite value in this same truth-table evaluation.
The actual native partial effect determines whether there is a successor.
No canonical-prefix test is imposed on a raw IN patch.

Combine native core, finite effects, successor and receipt on their actual
physical identities. Preserve written effect order to determine final
values. Combine duplicate native target positions once; inspect repeated
roles as often as their ordered stencil specifies. Assign the distinct
designated existing target bits in first-role/track order, whether or not
their final values differ. Construct core cells or the fresh finite bit
before the receipt cell, with fixed template-role order. Update the
actual affected head links. Unmentioned tracks, latches and locations
persist.

Order entries by version/finite pattern, decoded row, byte pattern,
alias partition and input bit; use absent before 0 before 1, ascending
port/latch order and ARC's symbol order. Flatten original row code,
tested pattern, guarded walks, label code, assignment lists and template
incidences using SSA Definition 3.2's unary/list encoding. This defines
a literal finite table $\Pi_U$ and its finite description length
$d_U$. Unbounded bank operations and Step74 remain their expanded native
rows; this table has no Cover, Call, string assignment or replay leaf.

